<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thirumalai Nayak Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1636">1636</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thirumalai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> Palace is a 17th-century palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, built around 1636 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirumala-nayak">Tirumala Nayak</a>, ruler of the Madurai Nayak kingdom. Built in a blend of Dravidian and Islamic styles, it is known for its huge columns, domes and stucco work. Only part of the original complex survives, and it is now a protected monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thirumalai-nayak-palace.jpg" alt="Thirumalai Nayak Palace" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: எஸ்ஸார் · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madurai_Nayak_Palace_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
